# Inline (anonymous) subscope call — stays refused (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3)

A *declared* subscope now lowers (see `subscope.catala_en`): it collapses to
one object creation plus a navigated read, keyed by the creation-per-subject
key. An *inline* call — `(output of Inner with {…}).b` used directly in an
expression, with no declared subscope variable — mints an anonymous instance
per occurrence, which that key cannot carry. Only declared subscopes lower;
the inline/anonymous form (the tutorial-2-1 shape) stays refused.

```catala
declaration scope Inner:
  input a content integer
  output b content integer

scope Inner:
  definition b equals a + 1

declaration scope Outer:
  input seed content integer
  output r content integer

scope Outer:
  definition r equals (output of Inner with { -- a: seed }).b
```
